{
  "description": "teamrig: load the team rules at session start and give them to each helper as it starts, ask before a push to a protected branch and refuse a force-push or delete of one, refuse a package runner that would fetch and run a package outside the project's lockfile (npx of a tool not installed, npm create, pnpm dlx, yarn dlx), ask before a hand-run database write, or refuse it as the team set, so the owner sees counts or a preview first, refuse a `teamrig exec` review (approve, refuse, escalate) that a tool call runs as anyone but the tab's own session, refuse a `teamrig owner` note or next from any tool call, as it acts as the owner, hold once a message that would wake an idle session cold, hold every message to the lead but a CRITICAL one while the owner's daily meeting is open, replace each secret a Bash, PowerShell, Read or Grep result holds before the model and the transcript see it, answer a send that was not delivered with the inbox line to write instead, tell a session whose shell no longer finds the bare teamrig command to run the installed copy by its path, remind each helper launch that work stays in the session by default, ask before or refuse one past the daily budget or in quiet hours as the team set, remind a session of unread inbox lines, ask a session once per turn to batch when it runs single-step calls in a row, record a Claude Code rename of the session as its team name, write an /effort the user typed in a session to its launch entry in the team config and tell its lead, ask for a handover at a task boundary when a context refresh is due, wake a session /clear started from its refresh so it carries on, warn a session past its daily budget, send a session or helper back once to a skill edit Claude Code refused and it never redid, record each Claude Code session on the machine, in a team or not, so the restore after a reboot can reopen the tabs it closed, put a colored circle before each tab's title for what its session is doing (ready, working, waiting on the user, waiting on the user's decision, an API error, compacting) when the team turns tab status on, let a Bash or PowerShell line whose every command provably only reads run without a permission prompt when the team turns the read-only shell on, and refuse the question picker to every session and helper, and to the lead outside the owner's daily meeting, with the reason to decide it if it is the session's own, else record it on its task and go on, when the team turns the picker guard on, and, when the team turns asks off, refuse each permission prompt a teamrig hook or Claude Code would raise, with the reason to record the step as waiting for the owner and go on, and let a line that runs one of the session's own jobs (a merge, a deploy, an exec request, a worktree removal, a commit with its hooks) run with no permission check once every teamrig guard passed it. Its mod (register.ts) adds /teamrig <command>, which runs a teamrig command in the tab and shows its output with no model turn (a read at once, a write only when typed by the person), runs that /clear in the tab when the automatic restart asks, once the session is quiet, runs /reload-plugins in the tab once an installed plugin changed, while no turn runs, and wakes an idle tab when unblocked urgent work is handed to its session: a prompt under the plugin's name, nothing typed into the terminal, with the wake logged and its cost shown.",
